 ## Overview
-Bucket Size Computation computes the **Bucket Texture**, which stores the position (index) of the last voxel of each bucket (bucket boundary voxel) [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently identifying these boundaries on the GPU without incurring the high cost of texture fetches in vertex shaders, which are required to compare a voxel's bucket with the next voxel's bucket [S1, S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from direct approaches by splitting the computation into a fragment shader step (to identify boundaries) and a vertex shader step (to construct the texture), avoiding the inefficiency of vertex shader texture fetches [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Bucket Size Computation computes the **Bucket Texture**, which stores the index of the last voxel of each bucket (the bucket boundary voxel) [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently identifying these boundaries on the GPU without incurring the high cost of texture fetches in vertex shaders, which would be required to compare a voxel's bucket with the next voxel's bucket [S1, S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from direct approaches by splitting the computation into a fragment shader step to identify boundaries and a vertex shader step to construct the texture, thereby avoiding inefficient vertex shader texture fetches [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
